  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Masculinidades Alternas y Roles de Gnero entre las juventudes de la zona Maya de Quintana Roo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Maya youths facing violence from criminal groups in southern Mexico lack secure spaces to interact peacefully, overcome trauma from violence, and develop their leadership skills. At the IAF, we support community-led solutions to promote peace and security. Our grantee partner, Mxico y Caribe Jvenes, A.C. (Mxico y Caribe Jvenes) empowers young people in Chetumal, Quintana Roo to increase graduation rates, reduce gender-based violence, construct a culture of peace, and reduce the pressure on youths to leave their communities in search of other prospects. Grant activities include leadership and rights training, seed funds to implement action plans, awareness-raising events, and a documentary on how violence impacts young people.</narrative>
  </description>
